    narr:narration """The current state of the [Kestrelwood spectrograph](narr:Expr_1ForgetLifecycleTarget_3) is defined by a specific operational baseline of [88.4 MHz](narr:Expr_1ForgetLifecycleTarget_1). This technical assertion is framed not as an isolated measurement, but as a result of a [verification process](narr:Expr_1ForgetLifecycleTarget_2) that anchors the current performance against established [June reference plates](narr:Expr_1ForgetLifecycleTarget_4). The broader operational philosophy governing these updates holds that [calibration validity](narr:Narrative_InstrumentCalibrationVerifiedAgainstReference) is contingent upon this cross-temporal check, ensuring that instrument performance remains consistent across the entire observing band rather than relying on instantaneous readings alone. The documentation reflects a commitment to this standard, treating the calibration as a verified, reproducible state.""" ;
